Slavic mythology and folklore is known  for its unusual creatures and today we  will discuss three of my personal  favorites the dama voya house dwelling  guardian spirits often linked to a  family rather than the house itself the  appearance of the dama voice varies from  a small gray bearded elderly man  to a dwarf like creature with horns and  a tail he can often be found at the  center of the house underneath a stove  however the Dhamma void prefers to be  heard rather than seen the Dhamma voice  seeks to maintain order and peace  throughout the home if treated well he  will help with chores around the house  and has been known to bring good luck  leaving the Dhamma voids favorite food  such as milk bread and porridge is often  appreciated and will keep the house  spirit happy if a dumb boy is angered  they will behave much like a poltergeist  haunting the family and sometimes even  injuring pets and cattle a cold touch  from a dumber voice often foretells of  misfortune the snuffing out of a candle  or the visual manifestation of the  Dhamma boy can signify the pending death  of a family member  less she are spirits of the forest they  are the protectors of the forest and  anything inside the lessee are known for  having a strong bond of animals they are  often seen being accompanied by either a  gray wolf or a bear the Alessia  shapeshifters and they can transform  into any animal or plant in the forest  their natural form often resembles a  large man sometimes covered in leaves  they have long hair and their beards are  often made of living grass and vines  their long limbs and their grassy facial  hair means that the leshy camouflage  well and can often be mistaken for a  tree the less you stand their tallest at  the center of the forest the further  they stray the smaller they become once  they reached the edge of the forest  Valecia tiny and can even hide under  leaves less he may not be evil but they  are indeed tricksters they have been  known to mislead travelers and cause  them to become lost in their forest they  rarely cause harm to travelers but they  have been known on rare occasions to  have too much fun and accidentally kill  their victims  if one befriends alesci they will learn  the secrets of their magic farmers and  Shepherds would often give Leslie the  cross around their necks as a gift and  in return the less she would protect  their crops and sheep the Bannock is a  bathhouse spirit often obsessive  cleanliness the third or fourth room in  a bathhouse was often reserved for the  Bannock  the Banat could often invite demons and  forest spirits to share its bath there  were no Christian images allowed in both  houses as to not offend the Bannock or  its guests if a person interrupted a  banach while it was washing the Bannock  would often pour boiling water on them  or even strangle them in the steam the  Bannock had the ability to predict the  future you would stand with your back  exposed to the benek if your future was  prosperous the Bannock would gently  stroke your back  however if trouble lay ahead the Bannock  would strike of its claws if you've  enjoyed this video then please go ahead  and leave it a like consider subscribing  if folklore mythology is something that  interests you if you have anything you'd  like to discuss or have any ideas for  future videos then please go ahead and  let me know in the comments below as  always I've been your host mythology and  folklore explained  [Music]
 

